  "notes": "Derived from the past tense of やる (to do). Used independently as an exclamation of success or joy.\n\nOften elongated for emphasis: やったー！ The longer the vowel, the more excitement is expressed.\n\nUsed by all genders and ages. One of the most common exclamations of happiness in spoken Japanese.\n\nCONTRAST: しまった (oh no!) expresses dismay over a mistake — the opposite emotional reaction.",
